From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:27:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] D2: incremental ranked session ids for the session
 list, sidebar and project tree
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Design t_01a1d563324d7e8e §3 D2 (review R5, C3, C9), card t_01a1d59ed6d15f90.

- hermes_state_rank_memo: one per-store memo of ranked page ids, shared by every
  list_sessions_rich(order_by_last_active) first page (/api/profiles/sessions, /sidebar,
  /projects/tree and each slice). Clock = D1 session cursor + messages.id watermark +
  a session_rank_lowered counter (AFTER DELETE / active / timestamp-or-session_id
  rewrite on messages, own trigger prefix). Moved sessions re-rank prev page ∪ dirty ∪
  ancestors ∪ direct children with the exact query restricted to them; a removed or
  lowered page row, a lowered counter (delete, rewind), an untrusted cursor or a params
  change takes the exact path. Rows are re-projected every request.
- Exactly invalidated preview cache keyed on transcript_revision (both revision
  triggers verified), installed only by a reader whose clock generation is current.
- Preview SQL: SUBSTR before the newline REPLACE (identical result, half the preview
  cost on the hub's 10 KB worker prompts).
- Store LRU reserves profiles + 4 (hub serves 11 profiles; _MAX_STORES was 8).
- scripts/benchmark_rank_memo.py: 5k/23k scale (memo growth <= 1.09x vs exact 2.8x)
  and a replay mix (synthetic 0.75x, copy of hub bb-tuner store 0.55x, fallback 10.6%).
